 693+ 07AB              ; Unified guest memory interface
 694+ 07AB              ;
 695+ 07AB              ; Guest physical address is classified before selecting its physical backing:
 696+ 07AB              ;   00000-9FFFF / C8000-FDFFF : guest RAM, pages 44h-83h
 697+ 07AB              ;   A0000-BFFFF               : linear VGA aperture backing, pages 30h-37h
 698+ 07AB              ;   C0000-C7FFF               : VGA BIOS slot, pages 20h-21h
 699+ 07AB              ;   FE000-FFFFF               : system BIOS slot, page 10h (8 KiB image)
 700+ 07AB              ;
 701+ 07AB              ; The VGA aperture backend is deliberately a byte-linear staging layer over
 702+ 07AB              ; the first 128 KiB of the 256 KiB VRAM allocation. It is NOT yet IBM VGA
 703+ 07AB              ; plane/latch/read-mode/write-mode emulation. VGA register semantics are a
 704+ 07AB              ; separate implementation stage.
 705+ 07AB              ;
 706+ 07AB              ; All backing is reached through WIN3. A is the page bias for the address
 707+ 07AB              ; formula: page = (guest_high_nibble*4)+(guest_middle>>6)+bias.
